==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|fervour||Commonwealth}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|enm|-}}, from {{der|en|fro|-}}, from {{der|en|la|fervor||a boiling or raging heat, heat, vehemence, passion}}, from {{m|la|fervere||to boil, be hot}}; see [[fervent]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈfɝvɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-fervor.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|American spelling}} An [[intense]], [[heated]] [[emotion]]; [[passion]], [[ardor]].
#: {{usex|en|The coach trains his water polo team with '''fervor'''.}}
# {{lb|en|American spelling}} A [[passionate]] [[enthusiasm]] for some [[cause]].
# {{lb|en|American spelling}} [[heat|Heat]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|passionate enthusiasm}} {{l|en|fire in the belly}}, {{l|en|zeal}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|fervent}}
* {{l|en|fervid}}
* {{l|en|fever}}

